can fill the entire flank and abdomen.\n\nIn younger adults, the typical presentation is episodic flank pain following diuresis.\n\nUltrasonography is the initial diagnostic choice for most cases of hydronephrosis and UPJ obstruction. Since the condition is present intermittently, sonography during a\npainful attack is most likely to delineate the diagnosis.\n\n(Option A and B) Abdominal X-ray films and barium and follow through are indicated if intussusception is the suspected diagnosis. Intussusception can present with\nintermittent abdominal pain; however, most cases present within the first 2 years of life (2 months -2 years). This child is 5 years old. Moreover, flank pain is unlikely to be\na presentation of intussusception.\n\n(Options C and D) Electrolytes, BUN, and creatinine might be indicated for evaluation of kidney function but they are of little, if any, diagnostic value.","source_answer_status":"source_revealed","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"4224ab8e0fd75cc3c64128ced45dded55db3d764","duplicate_group_id":"exact-4224ab8e0fd7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"166c975e12d48471fcde","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Pediatric amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":15,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"d5b0465ae855ddb4f192","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 PAEDIATRIC (2).pdf","source_page":97,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"451f5fed8499db970d55","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook