indicated?','{"A":"A. An infant younger than 12 months of age.","B":"B. A6-year-old male child with a family history of urinary tract infection.","C":"C.A5-year old female child with family history of urinary tract infection.","D":"OD. An infant younger than 2 months of age.","E":"E. A2-year old child with allergy to penicillin."}','D','According to the Royal Children''s Hospital (RCH) guidelines, the following children with UTI
should be admitted to the hospital for intravenous antibiotics and close monitoring:

¢ Most of children less than 3 months
¢ Children who are seriously unwell, such as those with a toxic appearance or

dehydration.
e Oral antibiotics cannot be tolerated.

